`Store(path)` creates the parent directory, opens a SQLite connection, enables WAL, applies both SQL migration files, and creates UPDATE/DELETE rejection triggers for immutable tables: [store.py](../services/foundation/store.py#L32). Each transaction opens and closes its own connection; all connections enable foreign keys, FULL synchronous mode and 5-second busy timeout, and writes start with `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`: [store.py](../services/foundation/store.py#L45). The service constructs one Store when `create_app(Settings(...))` runs: [app.py](../services/foundation/app.py#L102). `server.py` reads `REMISSION_DATABASE` (default `/data/remission.sqlite`), `REMISSION_ORIGIN` (default loopback URL), and `REMISSION_WEB_ROOT` (default `/app/web/dist`): [server.py](../services/foundation/server.py#L5). Uvicorn launches `services.foundation.server:app` on port 8765: [service.Dockerfile](../tooling/foundation/service.Dockerfile#L18).

The stack launcher first runs the CLI seed in a one-shot service-image container, mounting the named database volume at `/data`; then it starts the API container with that same volume at `/data` and the observed volume read-only at `/observed`: [run_stack.py](../tooling/foundation/run_stack.py#L48), [run_stack.py](../tooling/foundation/run_stack.py#L58). The README also documents CLI use “inside the qualified service runtime with its database volume”: [README.md](../services/foundation/README.md#L14). Source therefore has both API and administrative CLI writers to the same SQLite file when operated against the same mounted database. Default app startup is one Uvicorn process; independently launched CLI/replay processes are another entrypoint. The learner gets only an observed volume, not the database volume: [run_stack.py](../tooling/foundation/run_stack.py#L56), [run_stack.py](../tooling/foundation/run_stack.py#L57).

