`apply_current_state` derives current safety from persisted event history visible inclusively at the supplied time, resolves lineage heads, and puts the patient into ASSIGN-09 for listed intercurrent-event kinds; it advances patient/state/eligibility versions, recalculates consent version, creates a decision and an unavailable pending-work row (`replay.py:103-115`). `current_safety` loads all event payloads via `history`, filters visible records at time (inclusive), resolves lineage heads, and returns non-retracted consent/intercurrent events (`workflow.py:45-61`). Approval and non-hold state transitions query this helper while holding their SQLite write transaction (`app.py:317-333`, `362-375`).

The direct `replay` path parses/preflights all entries, filters by cutoff, sorts by availability/phase/record ID and persists a run cursor. Per arrival batch it appends events, writes ingestion receipts, applies current state, and advances cursor transactionally (`replay.py:117-161`). `replay_export` verifies the export, preflights its histories, requires preexisting patient rows, excludes consent records from its entry list, and delegates to `replay` (`replay.py:164-181`).

## Current authority versus immutable/history reads

Current authority is the patient row's `state_json`, version fields and `current_decision` pointer, plus rows in events and current drafts/tasks; the panel/workspace reads that state/pointer. Event append and workflow updates create a new decision display and move the pointer (`replay.py:103-115`, `workflow.py:64-90`). Current permissions are fields persisted in this current decision display, rather than a separately computed GET-time result.

History GET `/api/patients/{patient_id}/history/{bundle_id}` returns the saved bundle display/hash (`app.py:269-275`); later outcomes are a separate read of records available after the saved cutoff (`app.py:277-285`). Event read is a payload lookup (`app.py:287-293`); task/job/receipt/draft reads are separate (`app.py:295-309`, `351-357`, `417-423`). Archive read checks patient owner and archive owner and returns stored payload/raw source with `read_only=True` (`app.py:189-202`). The store installs no-update/no-delete triggers on decisions, bundles, tasks, receipts, events, state changes, and archive rows (`store.py:41-43`).

